+### FIX1: retained row backing in the collection/reduction branch
+
+Independent review F1 (`task-54-d7-bootstrap-workspace-review.md`, SHA256 `e76661e52aa65cf2df043522fd5a097331b6e40d806408e1c93bb8b614cfae50`) identified that the original W_BSGS expression included Rows only in BabyBuild. The corrected second branch above explicitly retains `Rows(t,b_s)` alongside X and the collection/reduction work. The saturated BabyBuild expression is unchanged.
+
+At fixed BASE, `linalg.rs:812–825` creates xs and its Option rows; blocks borrow xs at 833/850, and giant results are collected/reduced at 872–885 before xs leaves scope. Thus the outer row slots and every completed inner row remain allocated during successful collection/reduction. A block returning Err does not consume xs: later blocks still run during collection, and row backing remains until the subsequent reduction propagates an error and exits the function. Partially completed row construction on an earlier error is already bounded by BabyBuild's saturated Rows term. No successful or failing prefix receives an early-release credit.
+
+For any shared nonnegative additive resource coordinate, write BabyBuild as `rho+B`, with `rho=Rows(t,b_s)`, and the post-build term as C. The correction changes `max(rho+B,C)` to `max(rho+B,rho+C)=rho+max(B,C)` before adding the unchanged common terms. This algebra holds coordinatewise and after a nonnegative additive lowering to a shared coordinate; it does not require rows to occupy a disjoint coordinate. In general, lowering does not commute with componentwise max, so a later lowering must either conservatively lower the established vector bound or lower each full retained-owner branch before taking its maximum. It must not omit rho from the post-build branch or assume the build branch dominates.
+
+Rows accounts for outer Vec row slots and inner Option<Ciphertext> slot backing; X accounts for separately owned baby ciphertext component/limb backing. When lowering to object layouts, an inline Ciphertext stored inside an Option slot is already included in that slot: do not add a second inline Ciphertext size from X. Retained row backing is explicit here, not silently assigned to ChecksAndCollectionMetadata. Primitive/error/collection-capacity/allocator envelopes remain unevaluated; this correction provides no physical-fit claim.
